        "runId": "ada-en-20261110-work-8cfa443091a8",
        "model": "GPT-6.1"
      },
      "text": "After breakfast, continue fishing off Flamingo.\n\nThe main fishing grounds are in the open ocean, where the water deepens quickly and large pelagic species are found, and closer to the Catalina and Brummel islands.\n\nIn deep water, you may encounter sailfish, several species of marlin, dorado, yellowfin tuna and bigeye tuna. Around the islands you can find wahoo, sierra mackerel, Spanish mackerel, bigeye trevally, Pacific sea bass and roosterfish.\n\nOvernight stays at **Tamarindo Diria**.\n\nBreakfast and lunch are included."
    },
